# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts sshd (backgrounded, NOT `-D`) with the vulnerable
# cipher/MAC configuration and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * sshd is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which makes the "edited
#     sshd_config but never restarted the daemon" case detectable — the live
#     KEXINIT still advertises the vulnerable algorithms until a real restart;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting sshd cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART sshd, not merely start it.
